    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273">

                <pb facs="0605" n="521" xml:id="pg521"/>

                <head>No. 269.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Presson to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Custom-house, gloucester, mass.,</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Collector’s Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 14, 1886</date>.
                        [Received August 16.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose affidavit of Capt. Reuben
                    Cameron, of schooner Golden Hind, of this port, who was forbidden to enter the
                    harbor of Port Daniels, N. S., for water. This being a clear violation by the
                    Canadian Government of the treaty of 1818, I respectfully submit the case for
                    your consideration.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>D. S. PRESSON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Collector.</hi></signed></closer>



